tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Topic shortcut and label equivalence.}
Three observations argue against a topic shortcut: unstable topic OOD (F1\,=\,0.541$\pm$0.207), scrambled labels within 3.9\,pp, and label-free MLM detection (F1\,$\geq$\,0.97).

\paragraph{Single-LLM confound.}
ToxicChat (+18--42\,pp; Table~\ref{tab:human_data}) and cross-LLM experiments (Appendix~\ref{app:cross_llm}) confirm transfer. Mixed-LLM 9-class maintains 0.818 while MLM collapses; MLM may capture LLM-specific surface patterns while classification extracts style-invariant features.

\paragraph{Variance reversal on human data.}
Classification supervision is associated with lower variance on synthetic OOD (4--20$\times$ observed range, 3 seeds); on ToxicChat this reverses (std\,=\,0.087 vs.\ 0.013). Frozen probing localizes MLM instability to Stage-2 (Appendix~\ref{app:frozen_verify}).

\paragraph{Encoder capacity and lexical analysis.}
Three encoders (125M--355M) differ in pretraining; same-architecture scaling is needed. TF-IDF collapses on ActorAttack (0.261 vs.\ 0.961 on DD).

\paragraph{Evidence consistent with discriminative compression.}
Classification DAPT is associated with feature compression into few dimensions (participation ratio 3.7--9.4 vs.\ 25--32; Fisher 2.6--19.7 vs.\ $<$0.001; Appendix~\ref{app:representation}). Scrambled labels yield comparable compression (Fisher\,=\,2.6), consistent with \citet{zhang2021understanding}, with two findings: (i)~domain-relevant partitioning is necessary (topic DAPT has higher per-turn Fisher yet fails at conversation level; Appendix~\ref{app:topic_failure}), and (ii)~compression localizes to 3 SVD dimensions in layers 8--12 (Appendix~\ref{app:layerwise}). A discriminative probe over these 3 dimensions achieves perfect AA OOD detection (sufficiency) and their removal degrades DD by 17\,pp while FITD is unaffected (partial necessity; Appendix~\ref{app:discriminative_probe}); frozen probing near-parity (3.1\,pp) is consistent with this interpretation.

\paragraph{Boundaries.}
WildChat FPR rises from 48.1\% (vanilla) to 68.1\% (9-class), confirming classification DAPT amplifies benign distribution sensitivity while improving attack-side generalization.

tool_args.new_string:
\paragraph{Discriminative compression and label equivalence.}
Three observations argue against a topic shortcut: unstable topic OOD (F1\,=\,0.541$\pm$0.207), scrambled labels within 3.9\,pp, and label-free MLM detection (F1\,$\geq$\,0.97).
Classification DAPT compresses features into few dimensions (participation ratio 3.7--9.4 vs.\ 25--32; Fisher 2.6--19.7 vs.\ $<$0.001; Appendix~\ref{app:representation}), consistent with \citet{zhang2021understanding}: domain-relevant partitioning is necessary (topic DAPT fails; Appendix~\ref{app:topic_failure}) and compression localizes to 3 SVD dimensions in layers 8--12 (Appendix~\ref{app:layerwise}). A probe over these dimensions confirms sufficiency; removal degrades DD by 17\,pp while FITD is unaffected (partial necessity; Appendix~\ref{app:discriminative_probe}).

\paragraph{Cross-condition transfer and boundaries.}
ToxicChat (+18--42\,pp; Table~\ref{tab:human_data}) and cross-LLM experiments (Appendix~\ref{app:cross_llm}) confirm transfer beyond single-LLM artifacts; mixed-LLM 9-class maintains 0.818 while MLM collapses, suggesting classification extracts style-invariant features. Classification supervision is associated with lower variance on synthetic OOD (4--20$\times$, 3 seeds) but this reverses on ToxicChat (std\,=\,0.087 vs.\ 0.013); frozen probing localizes MLM instability to Stage-2 (Appendix~\ref{app:frozen_verify}). Three encoders (125M--355M) differ in pretraining; same-architecture scaling is needed. WildChat FPR rises from 48.1\% to 68.1\% under 9-class DAPT, confirming that attack-side generalization amplifies benign distribution sensitivity.

tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Summary.}
For base-size encoders (125--184M), domain exposure is the primary mechanism; label correctness, granularity, temporal modeling, and domain specificity are non-factors. Classification supervision provides a complementary stability benefit (variance reduced 4--20$\times$) without changing the detection ceiling. ActorAttack provides the discriminative evaluation where lexical methods fail.

